        "**Circle ($x^2 + y^2 = r^2$):** A vertical line through $x = 0$ intersects at $(0, r)$ and $(0, -r)$. Fails the vertical line test. $\\implies$ **NOT a function** $[\\times]$.",
        "**Sinusoidal Oscillation ($y = \\sin x$):** Continuous periodic wave. For every $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$, there exists a unique $y \\in [-1, 1]$. Vertical line intersects exactly once everywhere. $\\implies$ **Valid Function** $[\\checkmark]$."
