        "From $-7 < x \\le 2$: Sign is negative on $(-7, 0)$ and $(0, 2)$, and zero at $x = 0$ and $x = 2$. Note that $x = -7$ is excluded (denominator). Thus, $(-7, 2]$ is valid.",
        "From $4 \\le x < 5$: Sign is negative on $(4, 5)$, and zero at $x = 4$. Note that $x = 5$ is excluded (denominator). Thus, $[4, 5)$ is valid."
