      "**Asymptotic Curve Sketching & Extrema of Exponential Families:** Sketching $f(x) = x^n e^{-x}$, analyzing the parity of $n$, stationary points of inflection, and asymptotic limits as $x \\to \\pm\\infty$.",
      "**Applied Single-Variable Optimization:** Constrained geometric optimization involving inscribed rectangles in semicircles, inscribed cylinders/cones in spheres, open tanks, inscribed rectangles in ellipses, and right triangles.",
      "**Multivariable Functions & Geometry of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ Surfaces:** Transition from $y = f(x)$ to $z = f(x, y)$; quadric surfaces including circular/elliptic paraboloids, right circular cones, spheres, cylinders, and planes; domain identification and level curve contour slices.",
      "**Homogeneous Functions & Euler's Theorems:** Degree $n$ identification via scaling $\\lambda$; Euler's First Theorem ($x z_x + y z_y = n z$); Euler's Second Theorem ($x^2 z_{xx} + 2xy z_{xy} + y^2 z_{yy} = n(n-1)z$); generalized $m$-variable forms; and the modified Euler's theorems for non-homogeneous composite expressions $f(z) = g(x, y)$ (yielding $x z_x + y z_y = n \\frac{f(z)}{f'(z)} = g(z)$ and second-order forms $g(z)[g'(z) - 1]$).",
